#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# complexes

#% text
# `complexes` is the domain of the complex numbers, for facts `element(x, complexes)` in `assuming` and `refine`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `element(x, complexes)` with a number `x` is decided at once: `true` or `false`. With a symbol it is a fact that `assuming` adds to the assumptions.

#% item
# Functions that use assumptions (`simplify`, `refine`, `power_expand` and the sign tests) take the domain into account.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
element(1 + im, complexes)
#% output
#= true

#% cell
element(pi, complexes)
#% output
#= true

#% cell
element(sqrt(-2), complexes)
#% output
#= true

#% text
# A symbol in the domain:

#% cell
assuming(element(z, complexes), simplify(z + z))
#% output
#= 2*z

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# A symbol alone is not decided:

#% cell
element(x, complexes)
#% output
#= element(x, complexes)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `element`, `assuming`, `refine`, `reals`
